# Probe.cs is regenerated with a fresh stamp on every build, so committing it
# would mean every -Bump shows up as a diff. probe.ps1 writes it; nothing reads
# it but the compiler.
/src/Probe.cs

# dotnet build output. These used to be covered by bare `bin/`/`obj/` at the
# repo root; those are anchored now (issue #33), so the rule lives where it is
# actually true -- beside the csproj that produces them.
/src/bin/
/src/obj/

# ...but fixtures/ is the exception: a verbatim slice of a real Editor.log that
# TrialLog.Tests.ps1 parses. The repo-root `*.log` rule exists to keep captured
# logs OUT, and this one has to be in, so the exception is written down here
# rather than left to whoever next runs `git add -f`.
!/fixtures/*.log
